# Engine live run page on phones

## What to build

The engine's live run page (`packages/graph-execution/src/web/page.html` plus `src/web/assets/*.css|js`) is what graph-manager shows in an iframe while a run is live, and what a user opens directly from the URL a `--web` run prints. Today it is laptop-only: the top bar is one line that never wraps (`shell.css:5-8`, `white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden`), so on a 390 px phone Abort is cut off; the phase pills wrap over the graph; the graph pans with one pointer and zooms only with the mouse wheel (`graph.js:315-349`), so two fingers do nothing useful; the full-screen panel below 900 px (`panel.css:29-34`) ignores the notch and home bar; and comment boxes in the diff can be wider than the screen. This slice makes the page work at 360–430 px wide and on touch screens: a two-line top bar below 600 px, a sideways-scrolling phase row, one-finger pan + two-finger pinch zoom + tap-to-select on the graph (with the zoom maths exported as a pure, tested function), safe-area padding on the panel sheet, diffs that scroll only inside their own box, and 40 px hit areas on `pointer: coarse` devices. Only CSS, `page.html` (both pages) and `graph.js` change; no server or API change. Desktop (600 px and wider, `pointer: fine`) must look and behave exactly as before.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/page.html` (lines 1–35) — the run page: viewport meta at line 5, `#topbar` children at lines 19–29 (`.title`, `.meta#runid`, `.meta#provider`, `.meta.mono#elapsed`, `.prog`, `#conn`, `.spacer`, `#summarybtn`, `#action`), then `#main` (`#graph`, `#phases`, `#summarycard`) and `#drawer`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/page.html` (line 5, and its `#topbar` from line 19) — the suite page; it loads the same `theme.css`, `graph.css`, `diff.css`, `diffview.css`, `shell.css`, `panel.css`, `comments.css` and has the same viewport meta. Change its viewport meta too.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/shell.css` (lines 1–81) — body grid (`grid-template-rows: 48px minmax(0, 1fr) auto` at line 3), `#topbar` (lines 5–22), `#phases` (lines 27–30, `position: absolute; flex-wrap: wrap; pointer-events: none`), `.pill` (31–42), `#reviewcard` (45–51, `width: min(560px, 40vw)`), `#drawer` (54–69), `#summarycard` (72–81).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/panel.css` (lines 1–39) — panel grid column; `@media (max-width: 899px)` at lines 29–34 makes `#panel` a `position: fixed; inset: 0` sheet; `.panel-foot` at line 35; `.panel-head` 48 px at line 14; `.panel-close, .panel-back` 28 px at line 17; `.panel-tabs button` 36 px at line 21; `.panel-body { overflow: auto }` at line 25.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.js` (lines 217–382) — the canvas controller: `MIN_K = 0.15`, `MAX_K = 2.5` (219–220, not exported today), `createCanvas` (234), `zoomAt` (267–274, keeps a host-pixel point fixed), pointer drag-to-pan (315–342, 4 px slop, `suppressClick`), wheel zoom (344–349), click-to-select via `[data-node-id]` (354–361).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.css` (lines 1–15) — `.canvas` already has `touch-action: none; user-select: none` (line 3); `.zoombar button` 28 px tall (line 13).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.test.ts` (lines 1–75) and `panel.test.ts` (lines 1–23) — how asset tests import the plain-JS modules: `import { clampWidth, readPanelState } from "./panel.js";` from a `.ts` test, vitest in the default **node** environment (no jsdom in this package), so only pure functions can be tested.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/diff.css` (line 2–3) — `pre.diff { overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre }`, `pre.diff div { min-width: max-content }`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/diffview.css` (lines 1–4, 22–29) — `.dv-bar button` (small), `.dv-seg`, `.dv-file`, `.dv-file > pre.diff { overflow-x: auto }`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/comments.css` (lines 3–4, 7, 9, 39, 79) — `.composer` (`width: 100%; max-width: 100%; position: sticky; left: 0`), `.composer-text` (12 px font), `.thread` (`max-width: calc(100% - 6em)`, sticky), `#rvbox textarea`. Because the row `div` inside `pre.diff` has `min-width: max-content`, `100%` can be as wide as the longest diff line, which pushes the box off a phone screen. `comments.js` (lines 314–411) only sets class names (`composer`, `composer-text`, `composer-foot`) and the textarea height, so no JS change is needed there.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/theme.css` — global `button, .btn` styles; tokens `--deep`, `--panel`, `--panel-solid`, `--border`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/runpage.js` (lines 427–455) — `#action` is the Abort/Close button, `#summarybtn`, `#conn` text is `Disconnected` or empty (it is the status dot).
- `packages/graph-execution/package.json` line 51 — `postbuild` copies `src/web/page.html`, `src/suite/page.html` and `src/web/assets` (minus `*.test.ts`) into `dist/`; no build step to change.
- `eslint.config.js` lines 13 and 19 — `assets/vendor/` is ignored and `no-undef` is off for `assets/**/*.js`.
- `TESTING.md` section "Web view (agent-browser)" (lines 54–77) and "Web UI checklist" (lines 100+) — how to start a fake run with `--web` and look at it.

## Patterns to follow

**Naming / file conventions:**
```
Plain ES modules with // @ts-check and JSDoc types (graph.js line 1). Pure helpers are exported next to the
controller and tested from a sibling *.test.ts (graph.test.ts imports "./graph.js"). CSS media queries go at the
bottom of the file that owns the selectors, like panel.css:29 `@media (max-width: 899px) { ... }`.
Phone breakpoint for this page: `@media (max-width: 599.98px)`. Touch: `@media (pointer: coarse)`.
```

**Existing zoom maths to reuse (graph.js:267-274):**
```js
const zoomAt = (f, cx, cy) => {
  const k = Math.max(MIN_K, Math.min(MAX_K, view.k * f));
  view.x = cx - (cx - view.x) * (k / view.k);
  view.y = cy - (cy - view.y) * (k / view.k);
  view.k = k;
  moved = true;
  apply();
};
```

**Existing pan (graph.js:316-342):** `pointerdown` stores `drag = { id, sx, sy, vx, vy, moved: false }`; `pointermove` starts panning after a 4 px move (`Math.hypot(dx, dy) < 4`), calls `host.setPointerCapture`, adds `.panning`; `end` sets `suppressClick = true` when it moved, so the synthetic `click` after a drag doesn't select the node under the finger. A short touch tap already produces a `click` (the browser fires it after `pointerup` even with `touch-action: none`), which the existing `click` handler at 354–361 turns into `onSelect(id)`.

**Test pattern (graph.test.ts):**
```ts
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { MAX_K, MIN_K, pinchView } from "./graph.js";
```

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/page.html` and `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/page.html`

- **IMPLEMENT**: line 5 becomes `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">`. Do not add `maximum-scale` or `user-scalable=no` (user zoom stays allowed).
- **GOTCHA**: `viewport-fit=cover` lets content paint under the notch, so the safe-area padding below is required in the same change. Inside graph-manager's iframe `env(safe-area-inset-*)` is 0, so it costs nothing there.
- **VALIDATE**: `grep -n 'viewport-fit=cover' packages/graph-execution/src/web/page.html packages/graph-execution/src/suite/page.html` prints both files.

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/shell.css`

- **IMPLEMENT** (base rules, all widths): pad the bars for the notch and home bar: `#topbar { padding: env(safe-area-inset-top) max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right)) 0 max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left)); }` (keep the 48 px row by changing line 3 to `grid-template-rows: calc(48px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) minmax(0, 1fr) auto;`), and `#drawer { padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom); }`. On a laptop all insets are 0, so nothing changes.
- **IMPLEMENT** (append at the end of the file):
```css
@media (max-width: 599.98px) {
  body { grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto; }
  #topbar {
    flex-wrap: wrap; white-space: normal; row-gap: 6px; column-gap: 12px; overflow: visible;
    padding: calc(6px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) max(12px, env(safe-area-inset-right)) 6px max(12px, env(safe-area-inset-left));
  }
  #topbar .meta { display: none; }
  /* line 1: title + status; line 2: progress, then the buttons on the right */
  #topbar .title { order: 0; flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  #conn { order: 1; }
  #topbar::after { content: ""; order: 2; flex-basis: 100%; height: 0; }
  #topbar .prog { order: 3; }
  #topbar .spacer { order: 4; }
  #summarybtn, #action { order: 5; }
  #phases {
    left: 8px; right: 8px; top: 8px; max-width: none; flex-wrap: nowrap; overflow-x: auto; pointer-events: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; scrollbar-width: none;
  }
  #phases .pill { flex: none; }
  #reviewcard { left: 8px; right: 8px; width: auto; top: 48px; bottom: 8px; }
  #summarycard { width: calc(100% - 24px); padding: 16px; max-height: calc(100% - 48px); }
}
```
- **GOTCHA**: the `::after` break element must be a flex item with `flex-basis: 100%` and `order: 2` so `.title`+`#conn` are line 1 and `.prog`, `.spacer`, `#summarybtn`, `#action` are line 2. `.spacer { margin-left: auto }` (line 12) then pushes the buttons right. Check `#action` (Abort) is fully inside the viewport at 360 px.
- **GOTCHA**: `#phases` gets `pointer-events: auto` only below 600 px so it can be swiped; on desktop it stays `none` so drags pass through to the canvas.
- **VALIDATE**: see the agent-browser recipe in "Acceptance criteria".

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/panel.css`

- **IMPLEMENT** inside the existing `@media (max-width: 899px)` block (lines 29–34): add `#panel { padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top); padding-left: env(safe-area-inset-left); padding-right: env(safe-area-inset-right); box-sizing: border-box; }` (merge into the existing `#panel` rule there), `.panel-foot { padding-bottom: calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }`, and for a panel with no footer: `#panel:not(:has(.panel-foot:not(:empty))) .panel-body { padding-bottom: calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }`. Also `.panel-tabs { overflow-x: auto; scrollbar-width: none; }` and `.panel-tabs button { flex: none; }` so a long tab row scrolls instead of widening the panel.
- **IMPLEMENT** at the end of the file (touch hit areas, desktop unchanged):
```css
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .panel-close, .panel-back { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; }
  .panel-tabs button { min-height: 40px; }
}
```
- **VALIDATE**: at 390 px, `agent-browser eval 'getComputedStyle(document.querySelector("#panel")).position'` returns `fixed` with a node selected.

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/diffview.css`, `diff.css`, `comments.css`

- **IMPLEMENT** (`diffview.css`): `.dv-file { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }` and `.dv-file > pre.diff, #panel pre.diff { max-width: 100%; }` so only the `pre` scrolls sideways (it already has `overflow-x: auto`). `.dv-bar { flex-wrap: wrap; }` so the toolbar (Unified/Split, etc.) wraps on a phone.
- **IMPLEMENT** (`diff.css`): `pre.diff { -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; max-width: 100%; }`.
- **IMPLEMENT** (`comments.css`, appended):
```css
@media (max-width: 599.98px) {
  .composer { max-width: calc(100vw - 32px); }
  .thread { margin-left: 0; max-width: calc(100vw - 32px); }
}
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .composer-text, #rvbox textarea { font-size: 16px; } /* iOS zooms the page on focus under 16px */
}
```
- **GOTCHA**: after these, at 390 px with the Changes tab open, `document.querySelector(".panel-body").scrollWidth <= document.querySelector(".panel-body").clientWidth` must be true and the page `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth`. If `.panel-body` still scrolls sideways because of some other wide child, add `overflow-x: clip` to `.panel-body` inside `@media (max-width: 599.98px)` in `panel.css`. Do not touch `.dl .addc` (the hover `+` button) behaviour.
- **VALIDATE**: the evals above via agent-browser.

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.css` and `shell.css` (touch hit areas)

- **IMPLEMENT**: append to `graph.css`: `@media (pointer: coarse) { .zoombar button { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; } }`. Append to `shell.css`: `@media (pointer: coarse) { #topbar button, #summarycard .card-close { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; } #topbar button { height: auto; } .drawer-strip { min-height: 40px; } }`. Append to `diffview.css`: `@media (pointer: coarse) { .dv-bar button { min-height: 40px; } .dv-trow { min-height: 40px; } }`, and to `runpage.css`: `@media (pointer: coarse) { #panel .fail button { min-height: 40px; } }`.
- **GOTCHA**: `pointer: coarse` must not depend on width (a tablet in landscape is wide and still coarse). Desktop (`pointer: fine`) sizes must not change.

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.js`

- **IMPLEMENT**: export the zoom limits: `export const MIN_K = 0.15; export const MAX_K = 2.5;` (lines 219–220).
- **IMPLEMENT**: a pure function above `createCanvas`:
```js
/**
 * The view after a two-finger pinch: the content point under the starting midpoint ends up under the current
 * midpoint, and the scale changes by the ratio of the finger distances, clamped to MIN_K … MAX_K.
 * Points are in host pixels. Returns `start` unchanged when the starting fingers are on the same spot.
 * @param {{ x: number, y: number, k: number }} start the view when the second finger went down
 * @param {[Point, Point]} from the two finger positions then
 * @param {[Point, Point]} to the two finger positions now
 * @returns {{ x: number, y: number, k: number }}
 */
export function pinchView(start, from, to) {
  const d0 = Math.hypot(from[1].x - from[0].x, from[1].y - from[0].y);
  if (d0 === 0) return { ...start };
  const d1 = Math.hypot(to[1].x - to[0].x, to[1].y - to[0].y);
  const k = Math.max(MIN_K, Math.min(MAX_K, start.k * (d1 / d0)));
  const m0 = { x: (from[0].x + from[1].x) / 2, y: (from[0].y + from[1].y) / 2 };
  const m1 = { x: (to[0].x + to[1].x) / 2, y: (to[0].y + to[1].y) / 2 };
  const cx = (m0.x - start.x) / start.k, cy = (m0.y - start.y) / start.k;
  return { x: m1.x - cx * k, y: m1.y - cy * k, k };
}
```
- **IMPLEMENT** in `createCanvas` (pointer section, lines 315–342):
  - Keep a `/** @type {Map<number, Point>} */ const touches = new Map();` of active touch pointers in host pixels (`ev.clientX - box().left`, `ev.clientY - box().top`), and `/** @type {{ start: {x:number,y:number,k:number}, from: [Point, Point], ids: [number, number] } | null} */ let pinch = null;`.
  - `pointerdown`: if `ev.pointerType === "touch"`, add to `touches`. When `touches.size === 2`: start a pinch with the two pointers (`start = { ...view }`, `from` = their positions), set `drag = null`, `host.classList.remove("panning")`, `suppressClick = true` (a pinch is never a tap), and `host.setPointerCapture(ev.pointerId)`. Ignore a third finger (no new pinch). With one touch pointer, keep today's drag code path (the `ev.button !== 0` check passes for a primary touch, `button === 0`).
  - `pointermove`: update `touches` for touch pointers; if `pinch` is set and both of its ids are still in `touches`, `const v = pinchView(pinch.start, pinch.from, [touches.get(id0), touches.get(id1)])`, assign `view.x/y/k`, `moved = true`, `apply()`, and return. Otherwise run the existing drag code.
  - Tap slop: replace the fixed `4` in `Math.hypot(dx, dy) < 4` with `ev.pointerType === "touch" ? 10 : 4`, so a finger that wobbles under 10 px is still a tap; the browser's `click` then selects the node via the existing click handler (a "tap on a node selects it").
  - `end` (`pointerup`/`pointercancel`): delete the pointer from `touches`; if `pinch` included it, set `pinch = null` (the remaining finger does not resume panning; `drag` stays `null` until the next `pointerdown`). Keep the existing drag end logic.
  - Wheel (344–349) is unchanged; it keeps using `zoomAt` and the same `MIN_K`/`MAX_K`.
- **GOTCHA**: `.canvas` already has `touch-action: none` (`graph.css:3`), which is what stops the browser from scrolling/zooming the page under the fingers; keep it. Make sure the class is on the host that receives the events (`host.classList.add("canvas")` at line 246 — it is).
- **GOTCHA**: the file is `// @ts-check`ed through `tsconfig.json` (`allowJs`), so JSDoc types must be correct; `Point` is the typedef at line 11.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck -w graph-execution && npx vitest run packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.test.ts` (or from the package dir `npx vitest run src/web/assets/graph.test.ts`).

### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/web/assets/graph.test.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: a `describe("pinchView")` block (the test lives next to `panel.test.ts`, importing the plain JS like it does):
  - Spread around a fixed midpoint: `pinchView({ x: 0, y: 0, k: 1 }, [{x:100,y:100},{x:200,y:100}], [{x:50,y:100},{x:250,y:100}])` → `{ x: -150, y: -100, k: 2 }` (the content point (150,100) stays under (150,100)).
  - Pan with two fingers at the same distance: from `[{x:0,y:0},{x:100,y:0}]` to `[{x:20,y:10},{x:120,y:10}]` with start `{x:5,y:5,k:1}` → `{ x: 25, y: 15, k: 1 }`.
  - Clamped: a 10× spread from `k: 1` gives `k === MAX_K` (2.5); a 10× squeeze from `k: 0.5` gives `k === MIN_K` (0.15); `MIN_K === 0.15` and `MAX_K === 2.5`.
  - Zoom keeps the midpoint fixed at non-1 start scale: start `{x:10,y:20,k:0.5}`, from `[{x:0,y:0},{x:100,y:0}]`, to `[{x:-50,y:0},{x:150,y:0}]` → `k = 1`, and `(50 - x) / k === (50 - 10) / 0.5` (i.e. `x = -30`), `y = 0 - ((0 - 20) / 0.5) * 1 = 40`.
  - Same-spot start fingers return a copy of `start` (not the same object).
- **VALIDATE**: `npx vitest run src/web/assets/graph.test.ts` from `packages/graph-execution`.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `page.html` and `suite/page.html` have `viewport-fit=cover`.
- [ ] At 390 × 844 and 360 × 740 on the live run page: `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth` is `true`; `#topbar` is two lines (`document.querySelector("#topbar").offsetHeight` > 60) with `.title` and `#conn` on the first line and `.prog` + the buttons on the second; `#action` (Abort) is visible and `getBoundingClientRect().right <= innerWidth`; `.meta` elements are `display: none`.
- [ ] At 390 px `#phases` is one row: `getComputedStyle(document.querySelector("#phases")).flexWrap === "nowrap"`, `overflowX === "auto"`, `pointerEvents === "auto"`. At 1280 px it is `wrap` / `none` as before.
- [ ] One finger pans the graph; two fingers pinch-zoom around their midpoint within 0.15–2.5; a tap (< 10 px movement) on a node opens its panel; a pinch never opens a panel.
- [ ] Below 900 px the panel is a full-screen sheet with `env(safe-area-inset-top)` padding on top and the footer (or the body when there's no footer) padded by `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`.
- [ ] With the Changes tab open at 390 px, the diff scrolls sideways inside its `pre`, `.panel-body` and the page do not; an open comment box is no wider than `100vw - 32px`.
- [ ] Under `pointer: coarse`, top-bar buttons, zoom-bar buttons, panel back/close, panel tabs and diff toolbar buttons are at least 40 px tall (and 40 px wide for icon-like buttons); comment textareas have a 16 px font.
- [ ] At 1280 × 800 with a mouse, the page looks and behaves as before (TESTING.md "Web UI checklist" steps 1–5 still pass: no page scroll, fit/zoom, panel width persistence, split diff).
- [ ] `pinchView`, `MIN_K`, `MAX_K` are exported from `graph.js`, and the new tests in `graph.test.ts` pass.
- [ ] `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` pass.

How to look at it on a phone viewport (do this; it is a UI change). From the repo root:

```bash
npm run build -w graph-execution
CLI="$PWD/packages/graph-execution/dist/cli.js"; FIX="$PWD/packages/graph-execution/src/__fixtures__"
REPO=$(mktemp -d) && git -C "$REPO" init -q -b main && git -C "$REPO" -c user.name=t -c user.email=t@t commit -q --allow-empty -m init
echo '{"task:3":{"attempts":[{"hang":true}]}}' > "$REPO/.git/fake.json"   # task 3 keeps running
cd "$REPO" && GRAPH_EXECUTION_HANDOFF=detached SSH_CONNECTION=1 GRAPH_EXECUTION_FAKE_SCRIPT=$REPO/.git/fake.json \
  node $CLI $FIX/diamond --spec $FIX/spec.md --provider fake --web
# prints: Started run <id> in the background: http://127.0.0.1:<port>/
agent-browser set viewport 390 844
agent-browser open http://127.0.0.1:<port>/
agent-browser eval 'document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth'
agent-browser eval 'JSON.stringify({h: document.querySelector("#topbar").offsetHeight, abort: document.querySelector("#action").getBoundingClientRect().right, w: innerWidth})'
agent-browser screenshot phone.png          # then read phone.png and LOOK at it
agent-browser click '[data-node-id="1"]'    # panel opens full screen
agent-browser screenshot panel.png
agent-browser set viewport 360 740 && agent-browser screenshot narrow.png
agent-browser set viewport 1280 800 && agent-browser screenshot desktop.png   # unchanged from before
agent-browser close
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/abort; curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/close   # clean up
```

`agent-browser set viewport` does not turn on `pointer: coarse` or touch events in headless Chrome (checked with agent-browser 0.27: `matchMedia("(pointer: coarse)").matches` stays `false`, also after `set device "iPhone 14"`), so the 40 px rules and real pinch can't be seen there; the pinch maths is covered by the unit tests, and you can check the coarse CSS rules exist by reading the files. To exercise the pan/pinch code paths you may dispatch synthetic events with `agent-browser eval`, e.g. two `new PointerEvent("pointerdown", { pointerType: "touch", pointerId: 1, isPrimary: true, clientX, clientY, bubbles: true })` / `pointerId: 2` on `#graph`, then `pointermove`s apart, and read `document.querySelector(".canvas-svg").style.transform` before and after (`scale(...)` must grow).

